lign="top" style="width: 1.7in; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;12,326&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;     &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;Customer C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;9,161&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="43" valign="top" style="width: 32.15pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;9,211&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;     &lt;/tr&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;Customer D&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;6,223&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="43" valign="top" style="width: 32.15pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="163" valign="top" style="width: 1.7in; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="right" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: right"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;6,105&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;     &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/table&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;In addition to the concentration of revenue risk by customers discussed above, Rover has a customer with outstanding accounts receivable greater than 10% from all customers. This customer has transportation receivables of $9.6 million and $9.5 million as of December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0 0 12pt 31.5pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;14. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Fair Value Measurement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;The carrying amounts of cash and cash equivalents, accounts receivable, and accounts payable approximate their fair value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0 0 12pt 31.5pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;15. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Deferred Contract Cost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;In 2016, Rover acquired capacity on a third party pipeline that began July 1, 2016 and continued until the contract was terminated in December 2017. The payments are reflected as deferred contract cost on the balance sheet. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, the balances of deferred contract cost were $56 million and $63 million, respectively, in Miscellaneous deferred debits, Account 186. The deferred contract cost is amortized under straight-line method through the duration of the contract (November 30, 2033) and is recorded in Miscellaneous amortization, Account 425, in the statement of income. Amortization expenses were $7 million for each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0 0 12pt 31.5pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;16. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;The FERC's Revised Policy Statement on Treatment of Income Taxes Docket No. PL17-1, states that it no longer permits master limited partnerships including a company that does not pay taxes itself and is owned by a master limited partnership, to recover an income tax allowance in their cost of service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0 0 12pt 31.5pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;17. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Taxes, Other Than on Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Taxes, other than on income primarily consist of ad valorem tax paid on the assessed value of Rover's natural gas transmission lines based on fixed rates established by the applicable state or local taxing authorities. Ad valorem taxes are generally based on assessed property value at the beginning of each year. While Rover may protest assessed values with the taxing authorities, it bases its accruals on its assessment of the likely outcome on appeal.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Rover appealed the Ohio Department of Taxation's (the &amp;quot;Department&amp;quot;) final determination of the 2019 Ohio true value of Rover to the Ohio Board of Tax Appeals (the &amp;quot;BTA&amp;quot;) on September 11, 2020. On March 7, 2024, the BTA remanded the matter to the Department to redetermine the Ohio true value of Rover consistent with the opinion of the appraiser the Department engaged for purposes of the BTA hearing. Rover appealed the BTA's order to the Ohio Supreme Court on April 5, 2024, and the court affirmed the BTA's order on August 13, 2025. In 2025, Rover accrued additional property taxes related to the 2019 tax year of $43.1 million and interest of $26.2 million as a result of the court's affirmation of the BTA's order. Rover timely petitioned the Department's assessments of its 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, and 2025 Ohio true values, and these petitions remain pending. If it becomes probable that the Ohio Tax Commissioner's preliminary assessments for tax years 2020 through 2025 are ultimately upheld, then Rover would recognize an additional Ohio public utility personal property tax liability for tax years 2020 through 2025 up to approximately $294 million, including interest. Rover intends to pursue all available legal remedies for the 2020 through 2025 tax years, and Rover cannot predict the outcome of these matters at this time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;On November 10, 2025, Rover filed a complaint against the Ohio Tax Commissioner in the Court of Common Pleas, Franklin County, Ohio. Rover is seeking a declaration that the Tax Commissioner's 2019 valuation approach, if applied to Rover's subsequent tax years, would violate certain protections afforded to Rover under both the Ohio and the United States Constitutions. The Tax Commissioner filed a motion to dismiss on December 8, 2025, Rover replied on January 15, 2026, and the Tax Commissioner responded to Rover's reply on January 22, 2026. On March 25, 2026, the Court of Common Pleas denied the motion to dismiss.This matter remains pending, and Rover cannot predict the outcome of this matter at this time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0 0 12pt 31.5pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt; text-decoration: none"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;18. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Commitments and Contingencies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Rover is subject to proceedings, lawsuits and other claims related to environmental and other matters. Accounting for contingencies requires significant judgment by management regarding the estimated probabilities and ranges of exposure to potential liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h1 style="margin: 24pt 0 12pt 13.7pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NOTE C - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;The following table provides a summary of associated transactions for the periods presented:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" width="578" style="width: 675px; margin-left: 0.2in; max-width: 1783.31px; height: 280px" class="e-rte-paste-table"&gt;  &lt;tr style="height: 13.5314%"&gt;   &lt;td width="343" valign="top" style="width: 257.4pt; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p style="margin: 0 0 12pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1)"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;      &lt;td width="235" colspan="5" valign="bottom" style="width: 2.45in; border-top: none; border-right: none; border-bottom: 1pt solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); border-left: none; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); padding: 0 5.4pt; height: 0.25in"&gt;   &lt;p align="center" style="margin: 0 0 12pt 0.25in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;, sans-serif; text-align: center; text-indent: -0.25in"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style=